    "narrative": "Our strongest offensive leverage today comes from **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Taylor Ward** (71.19), both of whom benefit from ideal matchup conditions. **Lawrence Butler** finds himself in the most favorable spot of the day, leading off against the vulnerable Sugano (4.93 xERA), with his dynamic platoon advantage providing a significant 13% boost. Similarly, **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive 16% park factor uplift and a favorable wind direction at the top of the order against Buehler. Meanwhile, **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) remains a high-floor utility play; despite the xERA of Rodriguez being relatively average, **Jonathan Aranda**\u2019s 0.378 xwOBA and platoon advantage make him a critical asset for our batting average and on-base stability today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was keeping **Bryson Stott** (37.77) on the bench. He hovered near the 40.0 threshold, but a tough matchup against Harrison (3.39 xERA) and a negative platoon split (L/L) caused his projected efficiency to crater, making him a clear sit compared to the upside offered by **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.29) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (68.45). While **Jeremiah Jackson** hits from the #8 spot, his 16% park boost and the wind blowing out were enough to keep him in the lineup. Conversely, **Drew Gilbert** (40.12) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.33) are operating near their floors today against Rolison; they remain in the lineup only due to the lack of viable alternatives while we navigate the ongoing absences of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Yainer Diaz**. \n\nWe are monitoring the weather closely, as the park factors\u2014particularly for **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Taylor Ward**, and **Gavin Sheets**\u2014are heavily reliant on the wind out. Should the wind shift or late weather patterns emerge, our efficiency scores could drop rapidly for these hitters. We continue to hold **Will Smith**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Ryan Waldschmidt** in reserve, ready to deploy if the late-afternoon lineups shift or if we decide to chase stolen base upside in lower-projected slots.",
